From 5bed7aa4274ef6f96f78b06cbbe868521b0de1fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yarldron <yarldron@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:25:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add raw exFAT volume image support

New Common::ExFatVolume reads a bare exFAT image (boot sector at offset 0) in
place, with lazy directory parsing, the volume's own up-case table, NoFatChain
and FAT-chained files, and ValidDataLength zero-fill. It plugs into the archive
layer as the ".exfat" format, so --game, the launcher scan and the existing
read-only /app0 mount work with .exfat files like they do with .zar.

Adds tests/ExFatTests.cpp (exfat_tests) with a spec-based image writer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
